WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.203
-Last night saw
the first major elections

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.705
of the Trump era,
and Democrats won big,

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.107
trouncing Republicans
in New Jersey and Virginia.

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:09.976
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:14.113
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:15.481
That's right.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.583
Democrats had major victories
in the governor's races

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.518
in New Jersey
and Virginia last night,

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:22.121
which means it's cool
to be a Democrat again.

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:26.158
Right, new New Jersey --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:29.128
Isn't that right, new New Jersey
governor, Phil Murphy?

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.764
♪♪

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.633
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:36.669
Oh, my God.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.271
Democrats are such nerds.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.607
He looks like
he just won a chess meet.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.940
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.076
But, hey, at least New Jersey
finally has a governor

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:46.846
who can catch air.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.748
But Democrats
can be forgiven a little

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.717
awkward enthusiasm because
they've spent the last two weeks

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:54.787
absolutely freaking out over
the governor's race in Virginia,

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:57.156
where it seemed like
Republican Ed Gillespie

00:00:57.156 --> 00:00:59.525
was gaining ground
on Democrat Ralph Northam

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:02.194
by running a Trump-inspired,
race-baiting campaign.

00:01:02.194 --> 00:01:05.164
Pundits a day before the race
were already gloomy,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.833
like this panel
on "Morning Joe,"

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.136
during which, Mika Brzezinski
could not contain her panic.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.270
-We're gonna go around
the table now.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.172
-Oh, no.
-Elections tomorrow.

00:01:13.172 --> 00:01:14.407
Let me just start
with this question.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.508
-I don't know.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:19.478
-Does anybody here think
that the Democrats

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:20.813
are gonna win the governorship
in Virginia tomorrow?

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:25.617
-I don't know, and I'm alarmed
that this is a question.

00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:27.286
-What about you?
-I don't think so.

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.055
-And is it
the Donna Brazille stuff?

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.090
What is turning people
at the last second?

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.159
-Do you think Ed Gillespie
or Northam wins?

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.194
-It doesn't look like
Northam wins.

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.496
-Oh, my God.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.931
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.466
-You got to love
how Mika sounds in that clip,

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:42.835
like she just heard
some dirty gossip about a friend

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.204
while holding a glass
of Pinot Grigio.

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.506
"Oh, my God!

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.242
With the pool boy?!"

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.643
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.679
So, even before
the results came in last night,

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.914
Democrats were certain
they didn't have a chance,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.418
which of course is how you know
they actually had a chance.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:02.188
They won, but at least
the Democrats were wrong again.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:04.557
In fact, Democrats went on
to victory in several states,

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.759
first, in New Jersey,
where Murphy, the Democrat,

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.127
overwhelmingly won the race

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.162
to replace
GOP governor Chris Christie.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:12.198
Christie is so unpopular
in New Jersey that,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.199
on election day,
he found himself bickering

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:16.569
with a voter on the street
over a local issue,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:20.005
merging a township and a borough
after he cast his ballot.

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:21.007 line:0%
-Anything else?

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.610 line:0%
Sure, ma'am!
Why not?

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.645 line:0%
Yeah.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.349
'Cause I can't.
-In eight years.

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:30.783
Well, as governor, I can't.
-So, why didn't you?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.051
-I can't.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.219
I understand.
You're so frustrated.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:35.822
And you know what?
The easiest thing in the world--

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.157
The easiest thing in the world
is to stand where you stand

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.460
and stand on the sidelines
and critique.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.362
Run for the township committee
of Mendham Township

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:44.664
and be the voice to do it.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.298
No, I know,
'cause that's too hard.

00:02:46.298 --> 00:02:48.801
It's easier --
It's easier to sit here --

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.135
It's easier to sit here
and complain.

00:02:50.135 --> 00:02:51.370
-It's whose hand
in whose pocket.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.404
-It's easier to sit --

00:02:52.404 --> 00:02:53.706
-And I don't have
the money like you.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.007
-Oh, really, I'm sure.
I'm sure.

00:02:55.007 --> 00:02:58.244
Easier to sit here and complain.
But you know what?

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.145
That's the joy
of public service.

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:03.650
It's serving folks like you that
is really such a unique joy.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.787
-Man, it's nice that success
hasn't changed Chris Christie.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:10.456
You know, the best thing about
Christie living in New Jersey

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.791
is knowing he'll never be able
to go anywhere in public again

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:14.494
without someone
giving him [bleep]

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:15.695
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.530
"Hey!"

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.632
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.534
Hey, Governor,
I got a bridge right here!

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.870
Let me raise it for you!
There you go.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:27.006
There's another one over there.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:29.775
There you go."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.211
"There you go.
You can cross from New Jersey,

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:34.013
right over to
go [bleep] yourself.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:40.953
There you go."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.256
And that wasn't the only
big result in New Jersey.

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.624
There was also the case
of a local Republican official

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:48.694
named John Carmen who mocked
the Women's March in January

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.229
with a Facebook meme that said,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.664
"Will the women's protest

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.066
be over in time
for them to cook dinner?"

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:56.235
And that inspired first-time
candidate Ashley Bennett

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:59.138
to run against Carmen,
and last night, Bennett won.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:00.906
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:05.144
-So now John Carmen will be home
in time to make dinner.

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.312
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.747
Though he doesn't look like
he'd nail it.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.949
"Good news, honey.
I made fire bread."

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.450
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.485
Democrats also had big wins
in Philadelphia,

00:04:13.485 --> 00:04:15.355
where a civil rights lawyer
who defended

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.924
Black Lives Matter activists
just became district attorney,

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.925
and in Maine,
where voters overwhelmingly

00:04:19.925 --> 00:04:22.094
approved a ballot measure
to expand Medicaid

00:04:22.094 --> 00:04:25.130
over the objections of their GOP
governor Paul LePage.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.633
LePage vetoed the Medicaid
expansion five times

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.770
in support of President Trump's
attempts to repeal Obamacare.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.071
In fact, LePage made his name
by telling voters

00:04:33.071 --> 00:04:35.441
he would fight Obama's agenda
tooth and nail.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.921
-Well, last night, Maine voters
told LePage, "You first."

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.456
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.492
And let's not forget
New York City,

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.062
where the result, a win for
Democratic mayor Bill de Blasio,

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.230
was essentially guaranteed.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.164
But there was
an especially fun wrinkle

00:04:59.164 --> 00:05:01.033
in the fate
of former Fox News pundit

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.736
and Trump supporter Bo Dietl,
who ran against de Blasio

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.538
and has a history
of making racist comments.

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.373
Dietl got crushed last night,

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:09.641
which might've had something
to do with his closing message,

00:05:09.641 --> 00:05:12.512
a bizarre video
of him dancing on the subway.

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.712
-♪ No curses in my verses ♪

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:15.114
♪ Didn't have time
to rehearse this ♪

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.182
♪ We just came
to uplift your mind ♪

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.183
♪ Scratch the surface ♪

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.250
♪ Go ahead, Bo ♪

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:19.385
♪ Tell 'em what you know ♪

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.520
♪ All I know,
I love the street music ♪

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.123
♪ When I become mayor,
there'll be more street music ♪

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:27.159
Man, you got to love
New Yorkers.

00:05:27.159 --> 00:05:30.529
They know the first rule
of an asshole on the subway is,

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:32.198
ignore him
and hope he goes away.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.233
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:38.538
And with Bo Dietl, it worked.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:39.772
"Hey, I'm running for mayor.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:42.408
You guys want
to watch my dance?"

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:44.810
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.946
And Dietl has not been handling
his loss very well.

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:48.180
This morning, he took to Twitter

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.782
to attack the chairman
of a third party

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.217
that refused to endorse him,
tweeting,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.585
"Good morning, Frank Morano.

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:54.920
I lost last night, but I'm still
a multimillionaire.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.690
You're still a fat loser
in the loser Reform party.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.191
And you know
you're the real loser

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:01.159
when you can't even
spell the word "loser."

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:04.196
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:06.532
But by far, the biggest rout
was in Virginia,

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.033
and even aside
from the governor's race,

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.836
Democrats had
a huge night there.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:12.337
For example, a transgender woman
named Danica Roem

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:13.906
was elected
to the Virginia state house,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.241
becoming the first transgender
lawmaker in the country.

00:06:16.241 --> 00:06:18.677
And not only that,
she beat a Republican incumbent,

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:21.246
Bob Marshall, who sponsored
a transgender bathroom bill

00:06:21.246 --> 00:06:24.016
and once referred to himself
as Virginia's "chief homophobe."

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:25.617
He also refused to debate Roem

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:27.620
and referred to her
with male pronouns.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.221
The best part of Roem's victory
was her response

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.523
when she was asked
if she had anything

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.391
to say about Marshall
after she beat him.

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.826
Roem said,
"I don't attack my constituents.

00:06:34.826 --> 00:06:37.396
Bob is my constituent now."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:40.733
Damn.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.134
Damn.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:45.805
She threw so much shade,
his face turned even whiter.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.673
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:48.807
Virginia's also elected

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:50.475
the state's
first two Latina lawmakers,

00:06:50.475 --> 00:06:52.778
and in a truly shocking result,
a Marine veteran,

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:54.780
who calls himself
a Democratic Socialist,

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.682
upset one of
the most powerful Republicans

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.050
in the Virginia
House of Delegates.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.219
Republicans got beat
so bad in Virginia,

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.388
last night,
even the statue of Robert E. Lee

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.956
was chased out of town.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:10.195
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:12.331
By, apparently,
a very slow mob.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.001
And that's what's
especially interesting

00:07:16.001 --> 00:07:17.470
about last night's results
in Virginia,

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:20.339
because Gillespie very much
ran a Trump-inspired campaign

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:23.108
that openly embraced Trump's
racial-grievance politics.

00:07:23.108 --> 00:07:24.677
He aired ads connecting Northam

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.812
to the MS-13 gang
and sanctuary cities,

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:29.348
sent out mailers attacking
kneeling NFL athletes,

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:32.051
and made keeping up Virginia's
Confederate statues

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:35.087
a centerpiece of his campaign,
with ads like this one.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:37.523
-For governor,
there's a clear choice.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:41.327
Ralph Northam wants to take down
Virginia's Civil War monuments.

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:42.929
-I will do everything that I can

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:45.865
to remove the statues
at the state level.

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.934
Remove the statues
at the state level.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.703
-Ralph Northam
will take our statues down.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:53.004
Ed Gillespie will preserve them.

00:07:53.004 --> 00:07:55.841
-I'm for keeping them up,
and he's for taking them down,

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.110
and that's a big difference
in November.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:01.714
-November of 1866?

00:08:01.714 --> 00:08:02.982
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.982 --> 00:08:04.817
Trump, of course,
enthusiastically embraced

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:06.285
Gillespie's
race-baiting campaign,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:08.120
tweeting that
"Northam is fighting

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.489
for the violent MS-13 killer
gangs and sanctuary cities"

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:11.623
and that Gillespie

00:08:11.623 --> 00:08:13.925
"might even save
our great statues/heritage."

00:08:13.925 --> 00:08:15.727
Well, you'll never guess
how Trump feels about Gillespie

00:08:15.727 --> 00:08:16.962
now that he's lost.

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:19.365
Last night, he tweeted,
"Ed Gillespie worked hard

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.834
but did not embrace me
or what I stand for."

00:08:21.834 --> 00:08:23.202
Don't worry, Ed.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:24.704
Trump's only upset because
the election is still fresh.

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:27.006
The good news is,
in Virginia, when you lose,

00:08:27.006 --> 00:08:30.041
150 years later,
you get a statue.

00:08:30.041 --> 00:08:32.011
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:32.011 --> 00:08:34.179
Of course,
this is just one election night,

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:35.581
and there's still
a long way to go,

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.316
but last night's results
were promising

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.084
for a Democratic party
in desperate need

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.386
of something to give them hope.

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:42.255
And if there's one thing
Democrats are good at,

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:43.989
it's celebrating victories.

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.791
♪♪

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:48.127
Scratch that.
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:51.898
[ Cheers and applause ]

